Fatal error: Type of Drupal\acquia_search\Client\Solarium\Endpoint::$options
must be array (as in class Solarium\Core\Client\Endpoint).

search_api_solr 4.3.14 bumped solarium/solarium from ^6.3.7 to ^7.0.0.
Solarium 7 added a native `array` type to Solarium\Core\Configurable::$options
(and therefore to Solarium\Core\Client\Endpoint::$options). PHP requires a
redeclared property in a child class to carry the identical type, so the
untyped redeclaration in acquia_search fatals as soon as the class is loaded.

Adding the `array` type keeps the empty-array default (which intentionally
overrides Solarium's built-in host/port/path defaults) while satisfying the
covariance check.

--- a/src/Client/Solarium/Endpoint.php
+++ b/src/Client/Solarium/Endpoint.php
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@
    *
    * @var array
    */
-  protected $options = [];
+  protected array $options = [];

   /**
    * {@inheritdoc}
